# Architecture: Use Case Layer

- A use case must orchestrate one complete business scenario.
- Use cases must live under `app/modules/<module>/application/use_cases`.
- Use case classes must end with `UseCase`.
- Use cases must coordinate repositories and services through contracts.
- Use cases must enforce workflow-specific business rules and define operation order.
- Use cases must control transaction boundaries. Multiple repository operations in one workflow must commit together and roll back on workflow failure.
- Keep use cases independent from HTTP details, FastAPI objects, ORM query APIs, infrastructure implementation classes, and localized response text.
- Use cases may return domain entities, value objects, application DTOs, or explicit result objects that the API layer maps to response schemas.
